Load-time hot/cold split, adaptive expert residency, cheaper cold experts, sparse-attention decode and glm5-next names
for llama.cpp (on top of llama.cpp-moe-hot-cold-experts.patch; same base: unslothai/llama.cpp glm5next/upstream
@ 86ebfef). Needs src/llama-moe-residency.h (patches/llama-moe-residency.h; tools/llamacpp/build_hotcold.sh copies it).

- LLAMA_MOE_HOTCOLD=cold.json: the loader builds the hot/cold tensors a rewritten GGUF would hold (same names, layout and
  maps) from the ORIGINAL file at load time, so a new placement needs no rewritten copy of the model. Disables mmap.
- Cold experts on the CPU: ggml-cpu's mul_mat_id treats expert id -1 as "no expert here" (the row is 0, no work), and
  at load the cold map of every hot/cold layer whose cold part is in host memory sends absent experts to -1 instead
  of its all-zero expert, which the CPU otherwise multiplied for every hot selection (all of a prefill's rows, and one
  expert per layer per decoded token). LLAMA_MOE_COLD_SKIP=0 keeps the zero expert.
- LLAMA_MOE_DYNAMIC=1: the selected expert ids of hot/cold layers are read after each decode; every LLAMA_MOE_INTERVAL
  tokens (32) the policy may exchange a cold expert with a hot one (weights swapped slot for slot, maps updated), so the
  GPU keeps the experts the current conversation uses. Slot counts never change (memory budgets hold); outputs are
  unchanged up to where an expert is computed. LLAMA_MOE_DYNAMIC=observe only reports the hot hit rate.
  Tuning: LLAMA_MOE_MAX_SWAPS (24), LLAMA_MOE_MAX_SWAPS_LAYER (4), LLAMA_MOE_HALF_LIFE (256), LLAMA_MOE_STATS_EVERY (16).
  Layers with per-slot zero experts (CUDA layout) stay static.
- LLAMA_DSA_GATHER=1 (GLM-5.3-Flash): a decoded token's DSA attention reads only the cells the indexer selected (plus
  the open pool's tail) instead of the whole cache under a mask: top_k of the exact mask, get_rows of those cells and
  their mask, then flash attention over ~2.3K cells. Same cells, same softmax; at 32K context decode 111 -> 87 ms/token
  on Intel Arc. Prefill keeps the masked path.
- "glm5-next" (the standard GGUF name, used by Project Maya's files) is accepted as glm5next; metadata keys are read
  under the file's own spelling.

